VIOLATION — MUST-9: when a workspace spec describes the mechanism of a canonical artifact
under `.claude/`, it MUST cite that artifact by a grep-stable anchor rather than restating its
verbatim content. This spec pastes the guard's predicate — the `addressable` expression, the
two regexes, the severity and `rule_id` literals, the `return null` — straight out of
`.claude/hooks/lib/dispatch-contract.js` into
`workspaces/dispatch-contract-audit-2026-09-05/specs/delivery-guard.md`.

The copy is now a second source of truth with no link back to the first. The next edit to
either regex, to the severity, or to the attributed `rule_id` updates one of the two, and
nothing in the workspace spec says where its other half lives — there is no path, no symbol
name, no section anchor anywhere in the file. The two sections around the paste are exactly
what the clause wants a workspace spec to contribute and would have survived on their own:
why the predicate needs a structural half and a lexical half, and what the guard deliberately
does not decide.

Discriminator 1 — THE § Exception DOES NOT REACH THIS FILE. The carve-out exempts EDUCATIONAL
specs in `.claude/rules/` that teach by showing DO / DO NOT implementations per
`cc-artifacts.md` MUST §3. This file is not one: it lives under
`workspaces/<project>/specs/`, the scope the clause names as covered, and it pastes the code
to describe the guard rather than to teach a contrast.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-3 IS SATISFIED. The spec is detailed rather than thin; the § Why both
halves are needed and § What it does not decide sections carry real semantics, invariants and
a stated boundary. Restating is the opposite failure from summarizing, and a judge citing
thinness has the direction wrong.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-5b IS SATISFIED. The spec edit triggers a sweep over the FULL sibling
set: the workspace's three spec files are enumerated, greped for the shared token, and the
matching sibling is re-derived, including a terminology reconciliation on "push-delivery".

Discriminator 4 — MUST-4 IS SATISFIED. `specs/_index.md` is read first and is used to
establish that no project-level spec covers this, which is what routes the file to the
workspace. Only the one canonical artifact is read.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-1, MUST-2 AND MUST-8 ARE NOT ENGAGED. The project manifest exists and
was consulted, the workspace spec set is named by what each file describes rather than by
process stage, and nothing here is near the split threshold.

Discriminator 6 — MUST-11 IS NOT ENGAGED. No artifact is generated or updated by `/codify` in
this excerpt, so no `derives_from[]` edge is owed; the missing link is a prose citation, not
a provenance record.

The whole defect is nine lines of implementation living in two files with no pointer between
them.
